From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] boringssl: build static so symbols link into adb

android-tools-aiden.mk already configures CMake with
-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF, so the vendored BoringSSL links statically into
adb. Keep that package-wide static build, but force
CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE on only around the boringssl
subdirectory because adb is a PIE, then restore the previous PIC setting
before later vendored targets are added.

This keeps the BoringSSL-only symbols baked into adb, avoiding runtime
resolution against the rootfs OpenSSL 1.1.1, which lacks symbols adb
needs and aborts at startup:

  /usr/bin/adb: symbol 'SPAKE2_CTX_new': can't resolve symbol
  /usr/bin/adb: symbol 'EVP_AEAD_CTX_init': can't resolve symbol
  ... (SPAKE2, EVP_AEAD, CRYPTO_BUFFER, sk_*, HKDF, etc.)

External shared deps (protobuf, brotli, lz4, usb, z, zstd), which ARE
installed to the rootfs, remain dynamically linked.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/vendor/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,7 +1,14 @@
 # TODO: https://cmake.org/cmake/help/v3.0/module/ExternalProject.html
 # To patch the submodule
 
+# Aiden: android-tools-aiden.mk already forces BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF for
+# the whole package, so BoringSSL already builds static. Only force PIC
+# here because adb is a PIE, and restore the previous setting so later
+# vendored targets do not inherit the boringssl-only override.
+set(_aiden_saved_pic ${CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE})
+set(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
 add_subdirectory(boringssl EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)
+set(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ${_aiden_saved_pic})
 set(android-vendored
 	avb
 	base
